    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0488" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.428/576</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lindsay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Polk</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 183</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the request of the Canadian Government I
                    have the honour to call your attention to the fact that the signature of the
                    Treaty between the United States and Great Britain concerning port privileges of
                    fishing vessels, lobster fishing, halibut fishing, and Tariff on fresh fish, the
                        draft<anchor n="4" xml:id="d408-f1"/> of which was prepared by negotiation
                    between Sir Douglas Hazen and the Department of State, is still outstanding. The
                    Government of the Dominion will be glad to learn at what date the United States
                    Government will be prepared to proceed to the signature of this Treaty.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Lindsay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
